# Documentation

- Describe current behavior and clearly label expected, proposed, or unverified behavior.
- Never claim a command, setup path, check, or compatibility result was verified unless it ran.
- Prefer short examples with repository-relative paths and portable command syntax.
- Keep links local and one level deep from skill entrypoints.
- Do not include secrets, personal machine paths, proprietary source content, TODOs, or placeholders.
- When documenting safety, state that safety is non-waivable and isolation mechanisms are not absolute boundaries.
